            <ArticleTitle>Patellar pain and incongruence. I: Measurements of incongruence.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>217-24</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In 150 normal asymptomatic knees, the average Q angle was 15 degrees. The patellar length was equal to the patellar ligament length, and the average congruence angle was -8 degrees. In 53 knees with recurrent subluxation, the patella was high-riding (TP, 1.23), the sulcus angle was shallow (147 degrees), and the average congruence angle was +16 degrees. In 53 knees with &quot;chondromalacia,&quot; the Q angle was increased (20 degrees), and the average congruence angle was -2 degrees.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
